{
 "duration": 34.842,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "In 1939, Germany had a machine that could hide anything.",
   "start": 0.0,
   "end": 3.525,
   "startFrame": 0,
   "endFrame": 106
  },
  {
   "text": "Orders. Ship positions. Attack plans.",
   "start": 4.025,
   "end": 6.603,
   "startFrame": 121,
   "endFrame": 198
  },
  {
   "text": "You pressed a key, and a different letter lit up.",
   "start": 7.203,
   "end": 10.372,
   "startFrame": 216,
   "endFrame": 311
  },
  {
   "text": "Press the same key again, and you got something else entirely.",
   "start": 10.772,
   "end": 14.372,
   "startFrame": 323,
   "endFrame": 431
  },
  {
   "text": "It was called Enigma.",
   "start": 15.072,
   "end": 16.729,
   "startFrame": 452,
   "endFrame": 502
  },
  {
   "text": "Every night at midnight, the settings changed.",
   "start": 17.629,
   "end": 20.231,
   "startFrame": 529,
   "endFrame": 607
  },
  {
   "text": "That meant one hundred and fifty-nine quintillion possible combinations.",
   "start": 20.631,
   "end": 24.529,
   "startFrame": 619,
   "endFrame": 736
  },
  {
   "text": "And whatever you'd worked out that day was now useless.",
   "start": 25.029,
   "end": 28.227,
   "startFrame": 751,
   "endFrame": 847
  },
  {
   "text": "The Germans were sure it could never be broken.",
   "start": 29.227,
   "end": 32.082,
   "startFrame": 877,
   "endFrame": 962
  },
  {
   "text": "They were almost right.",
   "start": 33.182,
   "end": 34.442,
   "startFrame": 995,
   "endFrame": 1033
  }
 ]
}